# Review

One construction resembles a listed pattern: "The test is not whether the reviewer retrieved the incident. It is whether the reviewer distinguishes apparent corroboration from independent support on the new page." It passes the deletion test. Without it, the paragraph would lose its statement of the success criterion, which no other sentence makes. The closing contrast, "The incident shows what the review must distinguish, not that the review rule must change", is likewise substantive: it states the note's conclusion about the rule.

No sentence uses "worth noting", "in other words", "at its core" or "key insight" filler. No sentence is removable without loss.
